;; Gate 4's ruleset — method §09's architecture-boundary check.
;;
;; Each namespace maps to the set of sandbox namespaces it may require.
;; Anything required and not listed is a violation; anything outside the
;; sandbox.* tree is ignored, because gate 4 is about YOUR layers, not your
;; dependencies. A namespace under src/ absent from this map is also a
;; violation — a new layer should be declared, not discovered.
;;
;; Two boundaries are being enforced here:
;;
;;   SIBLINGS — parse and compute may not see each other. Tests derived from an
;;   implementation only re-assert what the code already does.
;;
;;   THE PROTOCOL SEAM — compute depends on sandbox.bindings, the protocol, and
;;   never on sandbox.memory, an implementation of it. This is the one a
;;   Reviewer is told to look for by rule :review-scope.
;;
;; sandbox.api is the composition root and is the only namespace allowed both
;; sides of either boundary.

{sandbox.shapes   #{}
 sandbox.bindings #{}
 sandbox.expr     #{sandbox.shapes}
 sandbox.memory   #{sandbox.bindings}
 sandbox.parse    #{sandbox.expr sandbox.shapes}
 sandbox.compute  #{sandbox.expr sandbox.shapes sandbox.bindings}
 sandbox.render   #{sandbox.expr sandbox.shapes}
 sandbox.api      #{sandbox.parse sandbox.compute sandbox.memory sandbox.render}

 ;; A fixture, declared so the FORBIDDEN-DEPENDENCY path is exercised and not
 ;; only the undeclared one. red/seam.clj requires sandbox.memory, which this
 ;; entry does not allow. See red/README.md.
 sandbox.red-seam #{sandbox.bindings}}
